 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-TYPE-DEFAULTS','meaning':'All72 complete type record objects retain every original property and omitted defaults. Actual Type constructor defaults rawName Unnamed,gender2,base_money30,skill=the effective base_money,flags[],threeBGMnil,suffix empty string. Explicit0 is retained; no editor9999 cap is a universal parser/constructor cap.','source_units':[0],'source_facts':['PC-F016']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-TYPE-GENDER','meaning':'Exact declared Male/Female/Unknown aliases map0/1/2. Unknown type is not female in the type record; normal trainer member creation attempts female for every nonmale trainer, while fixed-gender species reject that write. Owner conversion instead copies actual type gender2.','source_units':[0,1,2,7],'source_facts':['PC-F016','PC-F018','PC-F030','PC-F031']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-TYPE-NAME','meaning':'Type name localizes in TRAINER_TYPE_NAMES; ordinary runtime full_name joins type name and personal name unless type has_flag? NoName. That flag comparison is case-insensitive. It is distinct from exact-case AI skill-flag membership.','source_units':[0,2,5],'source_facts':['PC-F031','PC-F074']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-TYPE-LIVE','meaning':'Runtime gender/base_money/skill_level/flags facades consult current GameData TrainerType. These do not snapshot the English Name or recompute arbitrary AI strategy; AITrainer initialization separately copies current skill and flags.','source_units':[0,2,5],'source_facts':['PC-F031','PC-F074']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-MONEY','meaning':'Reached internal money-enabled trainer reward sums each opponent team maximum level times that opponent current base_money, then applies independent AmuletCoin/HappyHour doubles; wallet clamp precedes actual-increase stat/message. PayDay is a later separate stage. This states the exact source expression without evaluating a new business model.','source_units':[2,6,8],'source_facts':['PC-F031']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-LOAD','meaning':'pbLoadTrainer resolves type first, raises for unknown type, then exact type/name/version lookup; missing trainer returnsnil and hit calls to_trainer. No version fallback in that lookup. The20 complete current raw records and their member order are preserved.','source_units':[1,3],'source_facts':['PC-F017','PC-F018','PC-F030']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-MEMBER','meaning':'The complete to_trainer method creates/appends each member before later overrides. Exact form/move/ability/gender/shiny/nature/IV/EV/Shadow/ball order and constructor prerequisites use PC-F018 plus identity-stats-shop-reverse-addendum.v1.json. Existing original typed broaderchainOPEN wording is historical and resolves only those named propositions. No arbitrary load-event callback outcome is inferred.','source_units':[1],'source_facts':['PC-F018']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-RIVAL','meaning':'Rival-name replacement reads matching configured type then a String variable; the first match wins. It changes the new runtime trainer name, not the stored raw trainer record. Empty String remains a String for this test.','source_units':[1],'source_facts':['PC-F018']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-CHECK','meaning':'In nondebug mode both trainer type check and trainer check returntrue before lookup. In debug mode rejected missing type returnsfalse; load remains a distinct raising path. Missing exact trainer in loader and nondebug missing-trainer fallback are distinct returnnil versusraise stages.','source_units':[3],'source_facts':['PC-F030']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-DEBUG-PREFIX','meaning':'Debug new trainer can register and save trainer data before later PBS conversion/writer/message failure; no rollback guarantee. Free-version helper scans0..255 and returnsfirstmiss or-1. Real dialog/widget/media execution stays unobserved.','source_units':[3,10,11],'source_facts':['PC-F022','PC-F030','PC-F078']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-AUDIO-ORDER','meaning':'Ordinary trainer battle/victory selection takes the last nonnil field in supplied order; a stored empty String overwrites earlier field then falls back map/global/default. FromType instead directly preserves a nonnil empty field. Declared default records do not establish that an empty-string fixture can be authored by a particular blank PBS spelling.','source_units':[4],'source_facts':['PC-F032']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-AUDIO-PRELOAD','meaning':'Each correct next-battle preload clone wins for its own battle/victory/capture family; selection alone does not clear it. Map and global valid nonempty music precede distinct literal defaults. Converted audio request is separate from actual native sound.','source_units':[4],'source_facts':['PC-F032']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-INTRO','meaning':'Nil/empty type IntroBGM returns before memory writes or playback request. A valid intro preserves existing memory; absent memory prioritizes pending cue and clears delay with position0, otherwise remembers current BGM and current position with only the position query rescue0. Those writes precede playback and are not transactionally rolled back.','source_units':[4],'source_facts':['PC-F032']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-EXPORT','meaning':'Type SkillLevel getter omits values equal to base_money. Trainer writer preserves raw record iteration/member sequence and schema/sub-schema property sequence, skips nil getter outputs. Archive save/load and PBS text writing are separate operations; later write failure does not imply earlier registry/archive rollback.','source_units':[0,1,10,11],'source_facts':['PC-F016','PC-F022','PC-F078']},
 {'id':'PC-TRAINER-RELOAD','meaning':'ClassMethodsSymbols saves the whole DATA hash and replaces DATA on load; per-field projection/normalization is not present there. Game startup/load_all and ordinary save-data load are separate as complete PC-F078 states. Existing held records/AI/UI snapshots have no generic automatic refresh guarantee; native serialization/real reload remains unexecuted.','source_units':[11],'source_facts':['PC-F078']}
